W:2. To see him in his pride of growth, his robes are rich and green,
W:His head is speared with goodly beard, fit nigh to serve the queen.
W:And when the harvest time comes round and John is stricken down,
W:He’ll shed his blood for England’s good and for English men’s reknown.
W:
W:[Chorus:]
W:Hey, John Barleycorn, ho, John Barleycorn
W:Old or young, your praise is sung, John Barleycorn.
W:
W:3. The lord in courtly castle, the squire in stately hall
W:The great of name, of birth and fame on John for succour call.
W:He bids the troubled heart rejoice, gives warmth to Nature’s cold.
W:Makes weak men strong and old men young and all men brave and bold.
W:[Chorus:]
W:
W:4. Then shout for great John Barleycorn, and long may he prevail,
W:Let the toasts to him go  round and round in tankards of good ale;
W:Give me my native nut-brown ale, all other drinks I scorn,
W:For English cheer is English beer -- all hail John Barleycorn.
W:[Chorus:]
